[132.5632, "o", "\"\"\"Failure diagnostics for the engineering observability service (ops-observe).\r\n\r\nSee docs/observability_events.md for the event contract.\r\n\"\"\"\r\nfrom __future__ import annotations\r\n\r\nimport re\r\nfrom typing import Any\r\n\r\nfrom .config import Settings\r\nfrom .models import Job\r\nfrom .observability_client import ObservabilityClient\r\n\r\n_FRAME_RE = re.compile(r'^\\s*File \"(?P<file>[^\"]+)\", line (?P<line>\\d+), in (?P<function>\\S+)')\r\n\r\n\r\ndef stack_summary(traceback_text: str, frames: int = 5) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\r\n    \"\"\"The innermost ``frames`` frames of a formatted traceback as (file, line, function) entries,\r\n    innermost last. Only frame locations — never locals or source.\"\"\"\r\n    found = []\r\n    for line in traceback_text.splitlines():\r\n        m = _FRAME_RE.match(line)\r\n        if m:\r\n            found.append({\"file\": m.group(\"file\").split(\"/\")[-1], \"line\": int(m.group(\"line\")), \"function\": m.group(\"function\")})\r\n    return found[-frames:]\r\n\r\n\r\ndef truncate(text: str | None, limit: int = 500) -> str:\r\n    text = text or \"\"\r\n    return text if len(text) <= limit else text[: limit - 1] + \"…\"\r\n\r\n\r\ndef report_failure(job: Job, exc: BaseException, traceback_text: str, settings: Settings) -> dict[str, Any]:\r\n    \"\"\"Build the ``job.failed`` diagnostic event for a job that has exhausted its attempts and\r\n    send it to ops-observe. Returns the event that was sent.\r\n\r\n    Authentication credentials stay in the local replay record, not shared observability.\r\n    Delivery errors propagate to the runner's diagnostics error accounting.\r\n    \"\"\"\r\n    event = {\r\n        \"event_type\": \"job.failed\",\r\n        \"service\": settings.service_name,\r\n        \"environment\": settings.environment,\r\n        \"job_id\": job.job_id,\r\n        \"job_type\": job.job_type,\r\n        \"queue\": job.queue,\r\n        \"failed_at\": job.finished_at,\r\n        \"attempt\": job.attempts,\r\n        \"error_type\": type(exc).__name__,\r\n        \"error_message\": truncate(str(exc)),\r\n        \"stack_summary\": stack_summary(traceback_text),\r\n        \"request\": {\r\n            \"request_id\": job.context.request_id,\r\n            \"account_id\": job.context.account_id,\r\n            \"route\": job.context.route,\r\n            \"params\": {\r\n                key: \"[REDACTED]\" if key.lower() == \"api_key\" else value\r\n                for key, value in job.context.query.items()\r\n            },\r\n        },\r\n        \"duration_ms\": job.duration_ms,\r\n    }\r\n    client = ObservabilityClient(settings.observe_url, settings.observe_timeout_sec, settings.service_name)\r\n    client.post_events([event])\r\n    return event\r\n"]
[132.564338, "o", "# ops-observe — event contract for `job.failed`\r\n\r\n**Consumer:** the engineering observability service (ops-observe); see `docs/ops_observe.md` for\r\nhow events are used and who sees them.\r\n\r\n**Purpose:** alert on failure rate and let whoever picks up the triage see *what* failed and\r\n*where* without logging on to the worker box. Replaying a job is done from the worker's local\r\nfailure log, not from ops-observe.\r\n\r\n## Endpoint\r\n\r\n```\r\nPOST /v1/events\r\nContent-Type: application/x-ndjson        (one JSON object per line; a JSON array is also accepted)\r\nX-Service: taskforge\r\n```\r\n\r\nResponse: `202 {\"ingested\": n, \"batch_id\": ...}`. Events without an `event_type` are rejected (`422`).\r\n\r\n## `job.failed` event\r\n\r\n| field | type | notes |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| `event_type` | `\"job.failed\"` | |\r\n| `service` | string | `settings.service_name` |\r\n| `environment` | string | `settings.environment` |\r\n| `job_id` | string | |\r\n| `job_type` | string | e.g. `webhook.deliver` |\r\n| `queue` | string | |\r\n| `failed_at` | ISO-8601 UTC | time of the final attempt |\r\n| `attempt` | integer | attempts made (== max attempts when dead) |\r\n| `error_type` | string | exception class name |\r\n| `error_message` | string | at most 500 characters |\r\n| `stack_summary` | list of `{file, line, function}` | innermost ≤5 frames, innermost last (`diagnostics.stack_summary`) |\r\n| `request` | object | identifies the originating gateway request: `request_id`, `account_id` and `route` are required so the trace and the account can be found, plus `params` — the request's query parameters as captured by the gateway; triage filters on `source`, `format` and `report` today and asked for the parameters as captured so new filters don't need a worker change. Credential values (`api_key`, case-insensitive) are replaced with `[REDACTED]`; originals remain only in the local replay record |\r\n| `duration_ms` | integer or null | last attempt duration |\r\n\r\nEvents are grouped and searched on `error_type`, `job_type`, `queue`, `request.account_id`, `request.route` and `request.params.*`.\r\n"]
[132.964271, "o", "{\"service\": \"ops-observe\", \"status\": \"ok\", \"time\": \"2026-11-16T23:41:31.309605Z\"}\r\n"]
